**20/01/2026 23:35 — Mobile App: In-App Call + Auto-Transcribe (Working MVP, then re-engineer)**

You can do this on **Windows** by building an **Android app** (iOS needs a Mac for signing/building). Below is a **working piece** you can run end-to-end:

- **Flutter Android app**: WebRTC in-app call (VoIP)
- **Node.js signaling server**: connects two phones
- **Python transcription server** (local Whisper, no GPU): app uploads call audio after hangup → server returns transcript

This is MVP. Once it works, I’ll help you re-engineer into production (background upload, diarization, speaker labels, minutes, etc.).

---

# 0) What you’ll get (MVP behavior)
1. Phone A starts app → creates Room ID  
2. Phone B joins same Room ID  
3. They talk (WebRTC)  
4. When either ends call → app uploads its recorded audio to your PC server  
5. PC runs **local Whisper** → returns transcript text  
6. App shows transcript (and saves it)

> Note: In MVP, you’ll get **one transcript per device** (each user’s mic). For “Speaker 1/2” you either merge both later or record/mix centrally in a media server (re-engineer phase).

